SCOPE: `packages/yoru-contract/` — the canonical event schema + pairing wire
types shared by the yoru-cli (MIT) and the yoru server (AGPL-3.0). This
package is intentionally MIT: it exists so it CAN be safely imported by the
MIT `yoru-cli` — an AGPL-adjacent contract package would poison every
`pip install yoru-cli` the moment the CLI actually depends on it. It is not
yet a runtime dependency of the published `yoru-cli` wheel (consumed today
only inside this monorepo, by path); shipping it to end users requires
either vendoring its source into the CLI wheel at release time or
publishing it to PyPI separately — that's a release-tooling follow-up, not
done by this package's existence alone.

The SERVER (backend + dashboard + marketing + infra) is AGPL-3.0 — see the
`LICENSE` file at the repository root and `LICENSING.md` for the rationale.
